      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "blk_7e9fbc2967",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The repository front door: what the app does, the safety model, build/run instructions, permissions guidance, and the Ollama custom-path caveat. Points at this wiki and USER_GUIDE.md for the full walkthrough."
    },
    {
      "id": "blk_5926ce9a70",
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Coverage",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "blk_09196bcf0e",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Summarizes the three feature pillars (Ollama orphan audits, llama.cpp/GGUF management with dedupe, parallel disk scanning), the Trash-by-default safety model with the shared-layer guarantee, the CLT-only build path (scripts/build-app.sh, swift run for tests), Full Disk Access guidance for full scans, and the OLLAMA_MODELS limitation: the app reads ~/.ollama only, because a Finder-launched app does not inherit your shell's environment."
    },
    {
      "id": "blk_6888d3cf44",
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Key items",
